## Why This Is Asked
The question tests building a real-time, multilingual NLP system with strict latency, code-switching handling, and robust evaluation. It also probes deployment discipline and drift monitoring.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming NLP pipelines
- Multilingual encoders for NER/RE
- Code-switching and domain terms
- Latency governance, canary rollouts, drift dashboards

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: streaming inference skeleton
async function process(batch){
  const lang = detectLanguage(batch)
  const tokens = tokenize(batch, lang)
  const entities = nerModel.predict(tokens, lang)
  const relations = relModel.predict(entities)
  return formatEvent(entities, relations)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle out-of-domain terms and unseen entities?
- How would you monitor drift and trigger rollback?

